# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
#
# `.env*` keeps every real environment file out: `.env`, `.env.local`,
# `.env.production`, `.env.*.local` and anything else an operator might write a
# credential into. That breadth is deliberate — the cost of ignoring a file that
# should ship is one line below; the cost of tracking one that should not is a
# leaked secret that cannot be un-published.
#
# The negation re-includes **only** the template. It is the one `.env*` file
# whose entire content is placeholders, and a reader cannot configure the app
# without it. Per gitignore(5), `!` re-includes a path excluded by an earlier
# pattern as long as no *parent directory* is excluded — `.env*` matches file
# names, never a directory, so this re-inclusion is reliable rather than
# incidental. A future broad rule such as `.env/` would break it, which is why
# the release gate asserts the file is in the index rather than assuming it.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# 本地数据库（真实学习数据，绝不入库）
/data/

# E2E 产物与隔离数据库
/.e2e/

# 私有内容库：真实真题试卷、听力音频与图片。
#
# 为什么不入库：真题内容有版权、体积大（单套听力音频可达数十 MB），
# 且它是**用户本机的内容**而不是产品代码。仓库分发的是读取与校验它的程序，
# 不是内容本身。
/private-content/

# Export tooling output (staging workspace only)
/.public-export-manifest.json
